getNextNode() algorithm:

1. Save current = curr (this is what we return) [done]    

2. If curr has unvisited children (child_idx < childCount): [done]
    a. Push curr onto stack [done]

    b. curr = curr->children[child_idx]
    c. child_idx = 0  (reset for new node)
    d. return saved current

    3. Else if curr->nextSibling exists:
       a. curr = curr->nextSibling
       b. child_idx = 0
       c. return curr

    4. Else (dead end, need to backtrack):
       a. While stack_top >= 0 AND no more siblings at each level:
          - Pop stack, restore parent
          - If parent has nextSibling → go there
       b. If stack empty → return NULL (done)
       c. Else return curr

Edge cases to handle:
    - Root has no children → return root, then NULL
    - Last node in entire tree → return it, then NULL
    - Empty tree → return NULL immediately

Test mental model on simple tree:

root
├── section (data)
│   ├── decl1
│   └── decl2
└── section (inst)
    ├── label
    └── instruction
Call sequence: root → section(data) → decl1 → decl2 → section(inst) → label → instruction → NULL
